00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Episode 01 - 46 Linden Street

3
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:18,000
Excuse me.

4
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:20,120
My name is Richard Stewart.

5
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:21,240
I'm a photographer.

6
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:23,120
May I take a picture of you and your little boy?

7
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:24,040
What's it for?

8
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:24,900
It's for a book.

9
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:26,060
You're writing a book?

10
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:28,040
It's a book of pictures.

11
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:29,920
I call it Family Album, U.S.A.

12
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:31,920
Oh, that's a nice idea.

13
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:33,760
Well, it's fine if you take our picture.

14
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:35,200
I'm Martha Vann.

15
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,520
Thank you. I appreciate your help.

16
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:40,440
I'm Richard. What's your name?

17
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:41,320
Gerald.

18
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:42,600
How old are you, Gerald?

19
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,360
Five.

20
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:44,520
And where do you live?

21
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:46,200
We live in California.

22
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:48,560
Well, welcome to New York.

23
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:52,040
OK, just a second.

24
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,760
I'm almost ready here.

25
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:56,400
Can I help you?

26
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:58,600
Oh, please.

27
00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:06,380
Hold Gerald's hand, please.

28
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:10,160
Great!

29
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:12,600
Now point to the buildings.

30
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:16,620
Terrific!

31
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:21,520
Give Mommy a kiss, Gerald.

32
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,660
Nice!

33
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,500
Thank you, Gerald.

34
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:29,840
And thank you, Mrs. Vann.

35
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:31,160
Oh, my pleasure.

36
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:32,600
We'll be looking for your book.

37
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:36,080
Thank you. Good-bye. Bye, Gerald.

38
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:40,000
Thanks again.

39
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:42,200
Oh, you're welcome.

40
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:44,080
Hey, let me take your picture!

41
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:46,540
Wonderful. Please.

42
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,960
Are you from New York?

43
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:55,580
No, I'm from Greece.

44
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:57,600
I'm an exchange student.

45
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,560
When did you come here?

46
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:01,280
Three months ago.

47
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:03,360
Your English is very good.

48
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,600
Thanks.

49
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:06,940
I studied English in school.

50
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:12,520
Would you like some coffee?

51
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,960
No, thank you.

52
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:16,480
Tell me about your book.

53
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:18,560
Oh, it's not finished yet,

54
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:20,320
but I have some of the pictures.

55
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:21,280
Would you like to see them?

56
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:22,940
Yes. I'd like that.

57
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,200
Here they are.

58
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:29,300
Family Album, U.S.A.

59
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:32,640
It's an album of pictures of the United States:

60
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:35,680
the cities, the special places, and the people.

61
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:38,380
And these are pictures of people working:

62
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:47,600
steelworkers, bankers, police, street vendors,

63
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:53,420
ambulance drivers, doctors...

64
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:56,780
Oh, this is my father. He's a doctor.

65
00:04:58,980 --> 00:05:00,320
This is my mother.

66
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:01,620
What's her name?

67
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:02,680
Ellen.

68
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:06,160
My younger brother, Robbie.

69
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:07,700
He goes to high school.

70
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:10,260
This is my sister Susan.

71
00:05:10,260 --> 00:05:13,080
She works for a toy company.

72
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:16,080
Here's my grandfather.

73
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:17,720
He lives in Florida.

74
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:20,020
And this is my wife Marilyn.

75
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:21,560
Oh, she's very pretty.

76
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:24,600
Thanks. And what about your family?

77
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:27,600
They are in Thessaloniki.

78
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:30,200
That's a large city in northern Greece.

79
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:32,840
But now I'm living in the Bronx.

80
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:34,960
With a Greek-American family?

81
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:36,400
No. Hispanic.

82
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:43,720
Oh no! It's five thirty.

83
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:45,660
Will you excuse me?

84
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:47,640
I have to meet my wife.

85
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:49,280
It was nice meeting you.

86
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:51,200
It was a pleasure meeting you, too.

87
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:52,340
Thanks for your help.

88
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:55,440
And good luck! I've got to go.

89
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:56,740
By the way, I'm Richard.

90
00:05:56,740 --> 00:05:57,420
