I'm Robbie... Robbie Stewart.

286
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:15,240
I'm Alexandra Pappas.

287
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,600
How do you do?

288
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:20,880
Your brother left his bag of film on the ferryboat.

289
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:21,920
I found it.

290
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:24,160
I'm really glad to see you.

291
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:27,560
I mean... my brother'll be really glad to see you!

292
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:30,000
Robbie! Who is it?

293
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,840
It's Richard's film!

294
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:35,120
I mean, Alexandra Pappas.

295
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:37,160
Come in, please.

296
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:43,480
Alexandra!

297
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:46,020
Hello, Richard. I found your bag!

298
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:49,360
Oh, thank you! Thank you!

299
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:51,700
Um... Alexandra, let me introduce you.

300
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:53,120
This is my wife Marilyn.

301
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:54,980
Richard showed me your photo.

302
00:17:54,980 --> 00:17:56,000
How do you do?

303
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:56,960
Oh yes.

304
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:58,640
Richard told us all about you.

305
00:17:58,640 --> 00:17:59,880
It's nice to meet you.

306
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:02,000
And this is my mother, Ellen Stewart.

307
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:02,960
How do you do?

308
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:05,440
And my father, Dr. Philip Stewart.

309
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,920
Nice to meet you, Alexandra.

310
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:08,460
And... ah... you met Robbie.

311
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:11,920
Yes. And you must be Susan. Hi.

312
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:13,200
Hi. Welcome.

313
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:15,260
I'm so glad you found the bag

314
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:17,320
and took the time and trouble to return it.

315
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,860
Oh, it was no trouble.

316
00:18:18,860 --> 00:18:21,200
I just took the wrong train.

317
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,600
Would you like something to eat?

318
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:24,000
Thank you, no.

319
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,800
I'm late for dinner at my house.

320
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:26,720
I really have to go.

321
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:28,960
Would you like to call home?

322
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:30,560
I'd appreciate that.

323
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:32,320
Please, use the phone.

324
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:34,160
Thanks. Excuse me.

325
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:37,440
Alexandra is a high-school exchange student from Greece.

326
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,800
Where does she live?

327
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:40,720
With a family in the Bronx.

328
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:42,760
Oh, that's not too far from here!

329
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:44,420
Take it easy, Robbie.

330
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:46,560
Thank you.

331
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:49,840
I can only stay a few minutes.

332
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:52,080
Have some iced tea.

333
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:53,980
Thanks, Mrs. Stewart.

334
00:18:53,980 --> 00:18:56,000
Please sit down, Alexandra.

335
00:19:02,040 --> 00:19:05,000
So, you're an exchange student.

336
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,840
Where do you go to school?

337
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:09,400
At the Bronx High School of Science.

338
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:12,040
Oh, that's a very good school.

339
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:13,860
What are your favorite subjects?

340
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:16,260
Biology and mathematics.

341
00:19:16,260 --> 00:19:18,200
Richard tells me you're a doctor.

342
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,280
Yes, a pediatrician.

343
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:22,100
And what does your father do?

344
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:24,100
He's a lawyer, in Thessaloniki.

345
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:26,140
Would you like some pasta?

346
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:27,500
I made it myself.

347
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,380
It might be a little cold.

348
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:33,600
Thanks, no. I do have to go.

349
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:35,720
It was nice meeting you all.

350
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:38,100
Well, maybe you'll come for lunch some Sunday,

351
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:39,200
so we can really thank you

352
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:40,780
for bringing Richard's bag back.

353
00:19:40,780 --> 00:19:41,480
Maybe.

354
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:43,640
You're welcome anytime.

355
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:45,000
Good-bye.

356
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:52,640
Can I drive you home?

357
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:53,520
No, thanks.

358
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:54,800
The train is just up the street.

359
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:56,360
It won't take me long at all.

360
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:59,160
Well, you really saved the day for me, Alexandra.

361
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:00,200
Bye.

362
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:00,880
Bye-bye.

363
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:01,980
Good night.

364
00:20:10,320 --> 00:20:13,920
She's a smart young lady, and very nice.

365
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:17,780
Very! Hey, she forgot her bag!

366
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:20,920
I guess we'll be seeing Alexandra again.

367
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:22,900
Right, Robbie?

368
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:41,340
My name is Richard Stewart.

369
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,480
I'm a photographer.

370
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:46,560
I'm Martha Vann.

371
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:50,700
I'm Richard.

372
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:51,800
What's your name?

373
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:52,780
Carol.

374
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:56,060
By the way, I'm Richard.

375
00:20:56,060 --> 00:20:56,600
What's your name?

376
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:57,600
Alexandra.

377
00:21:08,780 --> 00:21:10,480
We live in California.

378
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:14,480
Are you from New York?

379
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:16,080
No, I'm from Greece.

380
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:25,420
I'm Robbie... Robbie Stewart.

381
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:27,500
I'm Alexandra Pappas.

382
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:28,480
How do you do?

383
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:33,400
Alexandra, let me introduce you.

384
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:34,680
This is my wife, Marilyn.

385
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:38,480
Richard showed me your photo.

386
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:39,600
How do you do?

387
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:44,160
Oh, yes, Richard told us all about you.

388
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:45,480
It's nice to meet you.

389
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:49,360
And this is my mother, Ellen Stewart.

390
00:21:49,360 --> 00:21:50,440
How do you do?

391
00:21:52,420 --> 00:21:54,720
And my father, Dr. Philip Stewart.

392
00:21:54,740 --> 00:21:56,280
Nice to meet you, Alexandra.

393
00:21:58,380 --> 00:21:59,800
And you met Robbie.

394
00:21:59,820 --> 00:22:00,440
Yes.

395
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:02,780
And you must be Susan.

396
00:22:02,840 --> 00:22:04,000
Hi.

397
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,400
It was nice meeting you.

398
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,760
Thank you.

